  "claim": "In borg_escape() danger levels 3.1, 4.1, 5.1, 6.1 and 8 combine the stair check (which queues '<') with the phase condition. On an up staircase a level-16 Warrior queued '<' followed by a Phase Door read (or, with the phase blocked by the anti-summon timer, a Teleportation read from the next step). The game took the stairs and then played the leftover keys on the new level, spending the scroll and, for Phase Door, moving the Borg off its arrival staircase before it had looked at the level. Making the stair escape a complete alternative queues only '<'; three controls are byte-identical, two of them through the changed condition.",
